      "category": "Text",
      "text": "As part of the evaluation of the Staggered Work Hours Program in lower Manhattan, the two project sponsors engaged Dr. Derek Phillips, Associate Professor of Sociology at New York University, to conduct in-depth opinion surveys. These were strictly anonymous, and sought to determine the genuine and unvarnished reactions of people to work schedule changes.",
